    "created_at": "2016-02-22T17:47:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-22T17:47:03Z",
    "body": "> How do we deal with IDL-defined objects then? Do they just need to patch HTML to become part of the big switch statement?\n\nHmm, I see. Maybe it could be two-tiered, with a switch and then a fallback to the [[Clone]] internal method? (Which, BTW, shouldn't take an _input_ parameter; if it's a method, it should use `this`).\n\nThe problem I see is that certain TC39 members are irrationally opposed to the existence of structured clone and will probably block it from ever being put in the spec. So if we do this kind of monkeypatch it'll be a permanent one.\n\n> And would you prefer the same for transferring? Defining everything inline? Seems rather messy.\n\nYeah, basically I'd rather avoid permanent monkeypatches.\n\n---\n\nAlso see https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-clonearraybuffer\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
