    "created_at": "2016-02-22T17:54:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-22T17:54:12Z",
    "body": "If you want to avoid adding internal methods we cannot add [[Clone]] for IDL-defined objects either, right? Or is adding internal methods to non-ECMAScript-defined objects somehow fine? I doubt it is. I'm personally fine with a permanent monkeypatch here given that this algorithm already lives in every ECMAScript engine. I'd rather specify it clearly, extensible, and bold than unwieldy as a thing that can be easily neglected.\n\nAnyway, if you prefer giant case/switch for everything I'll get on that tomorrow. It's less work though it'll require a bunch of specifications to upstream their structured clone extensions (which is arguably quite nice).\n",
